======== 4. what agreement to expect (computed from the printed intervals, before any comparison) ========
Monte Carlo SD of a 2.5% or 97.5% percentile bound from 10000 draws, if the bootstrap distribution is near normal with SD s: 0.0267 x s
Two independent streams then differ by SD 0.0378 x s; 95% of differences fall within 0.074 x s. Add printed rounding (half a unit in the last place).
cached opus R vs N       expect |ours - scorer| within: success 0.123 points, bill ratio 0.0039, time ratio 0.0080 (95%, before rounding)
cached opus R vs P       expect |ours - scorer| within: success 0.110 points, bill ratio 0.0030, time ratio 0.0029 (95%, before rounding)
cached opus P vs N       expect |ours - scorer| within: success 0.093 points, bill ratio 0.0043, time ratio 0.0103 (95%, before rounding)
cached sol R vs N        expect |ours - scorer| within: success 0.083 points, bill ratio 0.0037, time ratio 0.0060 (95%, before rounding)
cached sol R vs P        expect |ours - scorer| within: success 0.094 points, bill ratio 0.0028, time ratio 0.0026 (95%, before rounding)
cached sol P vs N        expect |ours - scorer| within: success 0.096 points, bill ratio 0.0042, time ratio 0.0059 (95%, before rounding)
Success bounds also move in lumps: one task flipping is 100/279 = 0.36 points, so a percentile can sit on a plateau and jump by a lump.

